# Shemá — the Admin's access surface (OBT-543 · docs/shema.md, "The Admin grants")
#
# Every route needs the `admin` role of the shema app ("Admin da plataforma"). Granting the
# Admin writes it in both apps, so an installation admin bootstraps the first one here:
# POST /access/grants with roleKey "admin". The routes, the shapes and every refusal sentence
# are in docs/shema.md §6.10. Set @accessToken after logging in as an Admin.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@accessToken = paste-an-admin-access-token

### One account by exact e-mail — roles per app, stored regions, what they reach
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/people?email=someone@example.org
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Grant a regional role with its regions (the regions are the account's whole scope)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/grants
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "USER_ID", "appKey": "shema", "roleKey": "coordinator", "regionKeys": ["africa"]}

### Grant a form seat — mesa and gestor never share an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/grants
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "USER_ID", "appKey": "resource-request-form", "roleKey": "mesa"}

### Revoke — the last regional role takes the regions with it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/grants/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": "USER_ID", "appKey": "shema", "roleKey": "coordinator"}

### Invite somebody with no account — the link lands on the PME's /convite page
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "someone@example.org", "appKey": "shema", "roleKey": "obtLab", "regionKeys": ["asia"]}

### The invitations nobody accepted, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/invites
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Recall one
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/invites/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"inviteId": "INVITE_ID"}

### Who granted or revoked which role or region, to whom, and when
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/access/changes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### What the invitation gives — anonymous, the form's route until OBT-549 moves it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-requests/access/invites/TOKEN

### Accept it, signed in with the invited address
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/resource-requests/access/invites/TOKEN/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{inviteeAccessToken}}
